plex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, but regarded as a show-off, not open to new ideas. Candidate B very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about colleagues. Candidate C can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further his education, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Candidate D responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper.\n\nWe need to discuss criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, calmness, cooperation, responsibility, etc.\n\nWe can argue that while B has strong reliability and stress, his nasty remarks and weak memory for numbers are concerning for crew cooperation and attention to detail. Candidate D has strong problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but hot temper and know-it-all attitude may affect crew cooperation. Candidate C has quick decision making, calm in crisis, technical understanding, but egocentric, communication difficulty, not willing to further education. Candidate A has anticipation, complex connections, leadership, but show-off, not open to new ideas.\n\nWe need to decide which candidate is best overall. Perhaps Candidate D might be better than B because D's technical competence and responsibility outweigh his hot temper, which could be mitigated. But B's nasty remarks are more severe for crew cooperation. Also B's weak memory for numbers could affect attention. So maybe D is stronger overall.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 3's recommendation of B and argue why we think D is better. Provide evidence: D solves problems extremely well (technical competence), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), can concentrate very well (attention), responds adequately to unexpected events (stress resilience). However D has hot temper and know-it-all (cooperation issues). Compare to B's nasty remarks (cooperation) and weak memory (attention). Argue that D's strengths outweigh his cooperation issues more than B's.\n\nThus we can change vote to D.\n\nWe must produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote D.\n\nLet's craft: \"I appreciate Agent 3's points, but I have concerns about B's nasty remarks and weak memory, which affect crew cooperation and attention. In contrast, D demonstrates strong problem solving, concentration, responsibility, and adequate response to unexpected events, which are critical. While D's hot temper is a concern, it is less detrimental than B's overt hostility. Therefore I recommend Candidate D.\"\n\nMake sure to reference explicit facts: \"B makes nasty remarks about his colleagues\", \"B has relatively weak memory for numbers\", \"D solves problems extremely well\", \"D can concentrate very well\", \"D takes responsibility seriously\", \"D responds to unexpected events adequately\", \"D has a hot temper\". Also mention criteria.\n\nProceed."}
